# Generated by `make ir` - regenerate rather than committing.
# These are per-platform (target triple) and per-optimization-level artifacts,
# and a committed copy shadows the Makefile rule that produces them: make sees
# an up-to-date .ll and skips regeneration, so a stale -O0 file silently wins
# over a corrected rule. See the IRFLAGS note at the top of the Makefile.
*.ll
